            "review_title": "Review at Swan Cafe & Bakery",
            "review_text": "Ravin Zhong\n31 contributions\n0\nCosy Comfortable Awesome\nSep 2019 • Business\nI first walked in January 2018, about the time it first opened doors. Swan is a famous brand in Japan. It's founded on the aim of supporting the unfortunate in life especially the disabled that have difficulties i finding a job to have a stable life. This immediately striked me as i begin to spend time here almost daily. It's my go to place for coffee or after dinner drinks. Once a while i tuck into the bakery fare. Nothing extraordinary but i am touched by the EQ behind this whole thing of supporting the unfortunate. It's worth the visit especially in the morning when you could just watch the world go by sipping coffee. \n\nI highly recommend the first floor for a good view. Good wifi connection is almost a regular feature for most cafes in Saigon. Compare with Kuala Lumpur, most cafes in KL need to improve on that wifi aspect if they are serious in attracting back the investments that they lost. \n\nThis is the rallying factor for Saigon or Ho Chi Minh city as some of you may like to refer to. There are some new cafes dotting the landscape on this street.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 13, 2019\nSwan cafe & Bakery\nThank you so much ^^\nWritten September 25, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
